# The ticket's flow: one POST with everything, one answer. Run the requests top to bottom
# (VS Code REST Client, Rider or Visual Studio). Every applicant here is made up.
#
# The images are tiny JPEG-shaped files with a plain-text marker inside; the IDNow simulator reads the
# marker. Real images work the same way: no marker means a valid document and a matching face.

@onboarding = http://localhost:5100
@image = /9j/4EFUTEFTIFRFU1QgSU1BR0X/2Q==

### Create and submit in one call. Waits up to 8 s and answers 201 APPROVED on the happy path.
# @name create
POST {{onboarding}}/v1/markets/MB/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "Tester",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-01",
  "nationality": "XB",
  "countryOfResidence": "XB",
  "identifier": { "type": "NATIONAL_ID", "value": "9876543210987", "issuingCountry": "XB" },
  "email": "applicant@example.test",
  "phone": "+15550100100",
  "documents": [
    { "type": "PASSPORT", "image": "{{image}}" },
    { "type": "SELFIE", "image": "{{image}}" }
  ],
  "termsAccepted": true
}

### The applicant reads it back with the token from the create response: status, next action, masked identifier.
GET {{onboarding}}/v1/markets/MB/applications/{{create.response.body.applicationId}}
X-Application-Token: {{create.response.body.applicationToken}}

### Which provider calls the application made, in order: identification, screen, account, card.
GET http://localhost:5300/_control/requests?keyPrefix={{create.response.body.applicationId}}
